From 73c016501ea6a066efd0705dbee0af7aa3fe59d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tencur <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 03:24:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] boot: create and write kennel's tables without the asserting
 exec

Kennel created its op1.db tables (op1rsettings, op1rplugins, euclid, dots,
the sq_store stores, tape markers, chord) and the seq_types ownership table
in op1_factory.db through db2::exec (0x0196F950), which asserts on any
sqlite error. A missing table needs free pages, so with the flash full the
OP-1 asserted at boot, every boot; the plugin crash marker then made every
other boot skip plugins without fixing it.

Tables are now created with op1_db_write. When that fails the store skips
its reads (db2's get asserts on a missing table too), starts from defaults
and is not saved this boot. The settings INSERTs in settings_store.c and
chord.c, and the seq_types ownership INSERT / DELETE, go through
op1_db_write too; a failed ownership step stops before seq_types is
touched. Same approach as op1r-src #72.

harness/settings_db_full_test.c runs kn_settings.c and settings_store.c
against a model op1.db at R246's addresses: 6/18 ok before, 18/18 after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
